IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cda-s11-s12-extent`

-- Criminal Damage Act 1971, sections 11(1), 11(11) and 12(1), (3), (6): TESTS.
-- Layer 1 tests. Every expected value below was written from the text before the
-- file was run. A failing assertion here would be a finding, not a value to be edited.

§ `Tests for sections 11 and 12`

§§ `12(1): when the Act comes into force`

-- s 12(1): the day it was passed is 14 July 1971 (the bracketed date under the long title). Expected: that day.
#ASSERT `the day the Act was passed` EQUALS (Date 14 7 1971)

-- s 12(1): three months beginning with 14 July 1971 end on 13 October 1971, so the Act is first in force on 14 October 1971. Expected: 14 October 1971.
#ASSERT `the first day the Act is in force` EQUALS (Date 14 10 1971)

-- s 12(1): the day it was passed. Expected: not yet in force.
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act is in force on` (Date 14 7 1971))

-- s 12(1): 13 October 1971, the last day of the three months. Expected: not yet in force (it comes into force at the EXPIRATION of the period).
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act is in force on` (Date 13 10 1971))

-- s 12(1): 14 October 1971, the day after the period expires. Expected: in force.
#ASSERT `the Act is in force on` (Date 14 10 1971)

-- s 12(1): 15 October 1971. Expected: in force.
#ASSERT `the Act is in force on` (Date 15 10 1971)

-- s 12(1): 1 January 2026. Expected: in force.
#ASSERT `the Act is in force on` (Date 1 1 2026)

-- s 12(1): 1 January 1971, before it was passed. Expected: not in force.
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act is in force on` (Date 1 1 1971))

§§ `11(1): arson at common law`

-- s 11(1): an act done on 13 October 1971, before the Act is in force. Expected: s 11(1) says nothing (the abolition takes effect with the Act).
#ASSERT `the status of the common law offence of arson` (Date 13 10 1971) EQUALS `section 11(1) says nothing about an act done before this Act came into force`

-- s 11(1): an act done on 14 October 1971. Expected: the common law offence is abolished.
#ASSERT `the status of the common law offence of arson` (Date 14 10 1971) EQUALS `abolished by section 11(1)`

-- s 11(1): an act done in 2026. Expected: abolished.
#ASSERT `the status of the common law offence of arson` (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS `abolished by section 11(1)`

§§ `11(11): repeals of enactments about procedure or jurisdiction`

-- s 11(11): inputs (about procedure or jurisdiction, repealed by s 11 or order, offence before repeal) = TRUE TRUE TRUE. Expected: continues to operate (all three conditions).
#ASSERT `the effect of the repeal of an enactment about procedure or jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `that enactment continues to operate in relation to the offence and to proceedings for it`

-- s 11(11): inputs (about procedure or jurisdiction, repealed by s 11 or order, offence before repeal) = FALSE TRUE TRUE. Expected: says nothing (not about procedure or jurisdiction).
#ASSERT `the effect of the repeal of an enactment about procedure or jurisdiction` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `section 11(11) says nothing about this`

-- s 11(11): inputs (about procedure or jurisdiction, repealed by s 11 or order, offence before repeal) = TRUE FALSE TRUE. Expected: says nothing (not repealed by section 11 or an order under it).
#ASSERT `the effect of the repeal of an enactment about procedure or jurisdiction` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `section 11(11) says nothing about this`

-- s 11(11): inputs (about procedure or jurisdiction, repealed by s 11 or order, offence before repeal) = TRUE TRUE FALSE. Expected: says nothing (the offence was committed after the repeal took effect).
#ASSERT `the effect of the repeal of an enactment about procedure or jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `section 11(11) says nothing about this`

§§ `12(3) and (6): extent`

-- s 12: England. Expected: they extend there (long title).
#ASSERT `whether the provisions of sections 1 to 10 extend to` England EQUALS `they extend there`

-- s 12: Wales. Expected: they extend there (long title).
#ASSERT `whether the provisions of sections 1 to 10 extend to` Wales EQUALS `they extend there`

-- s 12: Scotland. Expected: they do not extend there (s 12(3)).
#ASSERT `whether the provisions of sections 1 to 10 extend to` Scotland EQUALS `they do not extend there`

-- s 12: `Northern Ireland`. Expected: they do not extend there (s 12(3)).
#ASSERT `whether the provisions of sections 1 to 10 extend to` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS `they do not extend there`

-- s 12: `somewhere else`. Expected: this text says nothing about that place (no provision).
#ASSERT `whether the provisions of sections 1 to 10 extend to` `somewhere else` EQUALS `this text says nothing about that place`
